course: dictionary
lesson: 11518
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and alignment is one of them. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. «Check the alignment of the wheels before you drive.» Here the wheels are lined up in the right position, so they point straight ahead.
explain: «Tom used the text alignment button to centre his title.» Here alignment is about how writing is lined up on the page: left, centre or right. The words «text» and «button» are your clues. Always ask what the sentence is about, then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «When the planets are in alignment, they look lined up in the sky.» This is a space meaning, and the words «planets» and «sky» show it. «His plans are in alignment with the school rules» is different: it means his plans agree with the rules.
fact: Alignment means arranging things in a straight line or in the right position.
fact: «Planetary alignment» is when planets look lined up in a row in the sky, as seen from Earth.
fact: In computing, «text alignment» lines text up to the left, the centre or the right.
fact: «In alignment» means agreeing with something or being on the same side as it.
fact: «Out of alignment» means not lined up correctly, and «align with» means to line up with something or agree with it.
exercise: «Check the alignment of the wheels before you drive.» What does alignment mean here? | Feeling very tired after a long drive | A loud noise from the engine | *Arrangement in a straight line or in the right position | A type of bicycle bell
exercise: Tom used the text alignment button to centre his title. What does text alignment mean in this sentence? | *How the text is lined up on the page | Hiding words from the reader | Agreement with the school rules | Planets lined up in the sky
exercise: «His plans are in alignment with the school rules.» What does in alignment mean? | Very large and heavy | *Agreeing with, and on the same side as, the rules | Fighting against the rules | Hidden under the table
test: When planets are in alignment, what do they look like from Earth? | *Lined up in a row in the sky | Falling towards the sun | Spinning very fast | Hidden behind the clouds
test: Which phrase means not lined up correctly? | *Out of alignment | Align with | In alignment | Text alignment
exam: Jayden says alignment only means lining up wheels. What is the best answer? | Yes, but only in maths | Yes, that is its only meaning | *No, it can also mean planets lined up in the sky, or text lined up on a page | No, it only means planets
